    "sentence_translations": [
      "The Cooked Duck Flew",
      "",
      "The cooked duck flew!",
      "If a duck is already cooked, how can it fly?",
      "",
      "Actually, “the cooked duck flew” is a common saying.",
      "It is a metaphor for unexpectedly losing something you have seized, or failing to grasp an opportunity.",
      "For example, you participate in a running competition and run really fast.",
      "You think you will win for sure, but just before the finish line you take a fall and are overtaken by others.",
      "Then you can say: “I could have won. But since I celebrated too early, I fell and spoiled the opportunity!”",
      "",
      "“The cooked duck flew” is something very unfortunate.",
      "So in our daily life, even if we have a great chance of succeeding, we should still proceed with care, ..",
      ".. in order to avoid that “the cooked duck flies”!",
      ""
